From: FiyeroT <me@fiyero.xyz>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:41:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/71] hysteria, hysteria2, tuic, hooks in upstream files: a
 uTLS fingerprint is dropped with a warning

The lines of upstream files that "hysteria, hysteria2, tuic: a uTLS fingerprint is dropped with a
warning" needs; the feature itself is its patch of layer 03, in files of its own.

Pdk-Feature: hysteria-utls
Pdk-Zone: protocols
Pdk-Layer: 02
---
 protocol/hysteria/outbound.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/protocol/hysteria/outbound.go b/protocol/hysteria/outbound.go
index a8d26d23f..61111b51b 100644
--- a/protocol/hysteria/outbound.go
+++ b/protocol/hysteria/outbound.go
@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ func NewOutbound(ctx context.Context, router adapter.Router, logger log.ContextL
 		Context:        ctx,
 		Logger:         logger,
 		ServerAddress:  options.Server,
-		Options:        common.PtrValueOrDefault(options.TLS),
+		Options:        tls.QUICClientOptions(logger, common.PtrValueOrDefault(options.TLS)),
 		DomainResolver: options.DomainResolver,
 	})
 	if err != nil {
